  "c44_mentions_in_added_lines": [
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/teorth/optimizationproblems/pull/294.diff",
      "lines": [
        "+| [44](https://teorth.github.io/optimizationproblems/constants/44a.html) | Maximal number of relevant variables in Boolean functions of degree $d$ | 1.5 | 3.9819073803* |",
        "+- [44](https://teorth.github.io/optimizationproblems/constants/44a.html) **improved upper bound (unrefereed):** $C\\_{44} < 3.9819073803$* by [Ricardo Pinho](https://github.com/rpinho/c44-certificate/tree/c20385a7f74fddb5592c2224e4b5946c4435c121/local-degree-caps), 1 Nov 2026. Exact local-degree caps from a parity dichotomy on influences, with Fourier-granularity block-sensitivity bounds in Wellens's recurrence, retaining \u00c9pi's degree-48 data.",
        "+- **[P2026b]** Ricardo Pinho, *Exact local-degree caps and Fourier granularity in the relevant-variable recurrence*, 1 November 2026, unrefereed. [Written proof, certificates and checkers](https://github.com/rpinho/c44-certificate/tree/c20385a7f74fddb5592c2224e4b5946c4435c121/local-degree-caps). AI-assisted analysis."
      ]
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/teorth/optimizationproblems/pull/297.diff",
      "lines": [
        "+| $0.302825279490988$* | <a href=\"#T2026\">[T2026]</a> | $f(z,w)=A+B\\Delta(I-D\\Delta)^{-1}C$ with $\\Delta=\\mathrm{diag}(z,w)$, the transfer function of an exactly unitary $3\\times 3$ colligation with blocks $A,B,C,D$ and Gaussian-rational entries over a common 149-digit denominator, so $f$ is a Schur function on the bidisc. Exact integer computation of the 1681 coefficients with $0\\le j,k\\le N=40$ gives a finite majorant $\\sum\\_{j,k\\le 40}\\lvert f\\_{jk}\\rvert r^{j+k}\\ge 1+2.2\\cdot 10^{-42}$ at $r=3028252794909880/10^{16}$. Improves P2026 by about $1.0\\cdot 10^{-12}$. [Certificate and stdlib-Python exact checker, pinned commit](https://github.com/gomyway/c59-bohr-bidisc-certificate/tree/a014dc9455815c2875507017ebcd303b8da27b63); `c59_cert.json` SHA-256: `6d2e39e8741fb5e73593d4db007c68831243d32fe4ae298bc4fe750033ebedab`; `t7428_c59.py` SHA-256: `f78b73aad627ec446af3af00252631c00f482b9eb827109d99a783dc0cac7db4`. <a href=\"#T2026-ub-K2-0-302825279490988\">[T2026-ub-K2-0-302825279490988]</a> |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/teorth/optimizationproblems/pull/299.diff",
      "lines": [
        "+| $0.44667$\\* | [[Pin2026b](#Pin2026b)] | Uses D. Niedbala Giraudin's flux and half-diameter lemmas (PR #274, $0.446$) and keeps an angular coefficient term by a contact-moment estimate and an even outer factor, with $c=44667/100000$. Two interval checkers (Arb at 320 bits, mpmath at 340 bits) pass. Unrefereed, without independent human review or formalization. |"
      ]
    }
  ],
